<h2>Preview and planned data practices</h2>
<p>This page describes the planned calling service. The website preview does not establish that calls, verification, payments, recording, or moderation are operational. The operator, contact details, retention settings, and final privacy notice must be confirmed before launch.</p>
<h2>Who handles your data</h2>
<p>The proposed operator is {'{{COMPANY_NAME}}'}, at {'{{REG_ADDRESS}}'}. Privacy contact: {'{{CONTACT_EMAIL}}'}. Grievance contact: {'{{GRIEVANCE_EMAIL}}'}. These placeholders are not working contact details.</p>
<h2>Information needed for the planned service</h2>
<ul><li>Account and phone-verification details to identify users and connect calls; age and disclaimer acceptance timestamps.</li><li>KYC result, verified gender eligibility, provider reference, and verification date for host and restricted-lane eligibility. The design stores neither Aadhaar numbers nor KYC document images in our application.</li><li>Call participants, connection and end times, outcome, rate and billing for service delivery, settlement, and safety review. Call audio is not recorded or stored.</li><li>Payment and wallet entries, host earnings, reports, host blocks and private caller tags, AI safety flags, and complaint review records.</li><li>Service WhatsApp messages and replies used for call summaries, blocking, reporting, and caller tags.</li></ul>
<h2>No recording, live AI safety, and number masking</h2>
<p>Calls are not recorded and call audio is not stored. No human listens to live calls. AI follows each live call to detect harassment, abuse and scams by intent, ends violating calls and creates a safety flag; flags are reviewed before a strike is confirmed, and AI flags do not themselves impose a ban. See <a href="/recording-policy">recording and AI safety</a>.</p>
<p>Calls are designed to show a service number instead of the other participant's phone number. Masking does not hide numbers from the service or its telephony provider. Do not share personal contact details during a call.</p>
<h2>Providers and access</h2>
<p>The planned providers include Clerk for login, Didit and a licensed Aadhaar-verification vendor for verification, Vobiz for telephony, a WhatsApp Business messaging provider, and payment providers for UPI top-ups. The AI safety provider processes live call audio in real time only, without storing it. Their final selection, access controls, and data handling must be confirmed before launch. Access to call records and safety flags is restricted to authorised service and safety functions.</p>
<h2>Retention and requests</h2>
<p>No call audio is retained, because none is recorded. The backend specification keeps call metadata for at least 180 days. These are planned settings, not a statement that a legal retention obligation has been verified. Final retention periods, financial-record requirements, and any preservation for disputes or lawful requests must be disclosed before launch.</p>
<p>The planned process will let you request access, correction, deletion, or a review after identity verification. The <a href="/data-deletion">deletion page</a> explains the intended process and its current limits. This service is intended only for adults aged 18 or older.</p>
